On CHERI targets, set the maximum degree of bounds tightening for
userspace programs and libraries.
The default value is
.Li conservative
on CHERI targets and
.Li none
on other targets.
Each value adds bounds beyond the previous one:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li none
Don't try to set bounds.
In practice, this is the same as
.Li conservative
on CHERI targets.
.It Li conservative
Stack allocations
.It Li references-only
C++ references that are a fixed size
.It Li subobject-safe
When taking a pointer to a subobject
.It Li aggressive
Whenever feasiable and not annotated as unsafe
.It Li very-aggressive
On individul array entries in &array[index] expressions
.It everywhere-unsafe
Everywhere there is no opt-out.
.El
Individual program or library Makefiles opt in by setting
.Va CHERI_SUBOBJECT_BOUNDS_MAX
to a value other than
.Li conservative
before including
.In bsd.lib.mk
or
.In bsd.prog.mk .
.Pp
Values above
.Li subobject-safe
are likely to be unusable in practice.
